","The entropy change (\(\Delta S_{\text{rxb}}\)) for the reaction is calculated using the following formula:

\[
\Delta S_{\text{rxb}} = \sum m \ln S_p - \sum n \ln S_r
\]

where \(m\) and \(n\) are the standard molar coefficients of the products and reactants, respectively, and \(S_p\) and \(S_r\) are the molar entropies of the products and reactants.

For the given reaction:

\[
2 \text{PbS(s)} + 3 \text{O}_2(g) \rightarrow 2 \text{PDO(s)} + 2 \text{SO}_2(g)
\]

Substitute the given molar entropies and coefficients:

\[
\Delta S_{\text{rxb}} = \left[ 2 \times 66.5 + 2 \times 248.2 \right] - \left[ 2 \times 91.2 + 3 \times 205.1 \right]
\]

\[
