Molar fraction of urea = moles of urea / (moles of urea + moles of CCl4) = (0.6216 / M_u) / (0.6216 / M_u + 0.325)

The mole curve constant (K_m) for CCl4 is 5.52 C·kg/mol.

For naphthalene:
ΔT_AB = K_m * m_n
0.402°C = 5.52 C· kg/mol * (0.00400 mol) / (0.050 kg)
0.402 = 5.52 * 0.00400 / 0.050
0.402 = 0.4416
