   \]
   where \( \Delta(\omega) \) is the discrete delta function. Thus, the Fourier transform of \( 3\sin(2\pi t) \) is:
   \[
   F_1(\omega) = 3 \cdot \frac{j}{2} \left[ \delta(\omega - 2\pi) - \delta(\omega + 2\pi) \right] = \frac{3j}{2} \left[ \delta(\omega - 2\pi) - \delta(\omega + 2\pi) \right]
   \]

