","To find the probability that the number on the cell is a multi.p.....ple of 3 or 4, we can use the inclusion-extension principle.

The number of multiples of 3 from 1 to 30 is \(\boxed{\frac{30}{3} = 10}\). These are \(\boxed{3, 6, 9, \ldots, 30}\).
The number of multiples of 4 from 1 to 30 is \(\boxed{\frac{30}{4} = 7.5}\), so there are 7 multiples of 4. These are \(\boxed{4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28}\).

