   \]

   However, the pressure required to avoid cavitation is typically determined by the pressure required to avoid the vapor pressure at the inlet, which is the saturation pressure. For a clear pressure head, the pressure at the inlet must be higher than the saturation pressure by a depth of at least 1 meter (10 kPa).

   \[
   P_{required} = P_{atm} + P_{head} + 10 \text{ kPa} = 150.335 \text{ kPa} + 10 \text{ kPa} = 160.335 \text{kPa}
   \]

