- \( d = 10.0 \, \text{m} \)  
Substituting the values:  
\[
W = 60.0 \, \text{N} \times 10.0 \, \text{m} \times \cos 60.0^\circ
\]  
Since \( \cos 60.0^\circ = 0.5 \), the work done is:  
\[
W = 60.0 \times 10.0 \times 0.5 = 300 \, \text{J}
\]  
