\]

Let \( x \) be the moles of N₂O₄ and \( y \) be the moles of NO₂. The total number of moles in the gas is \( x + 2y \).

The average molecular mass of the gas is:
\[
\text{Average molecular mass} = \frac{\text{Mass of } \text{N}_2\text{O}_4 + 2 \times \text{Mass of }\text{NO}_2}{x + 2y}
